# What this test reaches for that no DEPS edge supplies (format
# `<path> <name>`). deep-deps mounts each of these RECURSIVELY
# DEEPENED at DEEP-DEPS/<name>, so a std entry brings its own deps
# (std/<e>/DEPS) with it and only what an edge cannot reach is listed
# here: a curry base, a hash bound as a literal, or a name the server
# or client looks up (design/caos-expr.md). A nested mount does not
# satisfy a BY-NAME lookup — flake-builder (the server, for any raw
# flake tree) and bash (std_image) are named even where an edge also
# supplies them. chat.rs also resolves /cas/std/runner by name, but
# only behind a --llm-bin/--bash-bin/--rgrep-bin override, which no
# test passes; one that does will fail loudly and add it here.
../../std/bash bash
../../std/bash-tool bash-tool
../../std/llm-step llm-step
../../std/cargo cargo
../../std/flake-builder flake-builder
../../std/llm-stub llm-stub
